From 03034f62baae21b93544e3a011a47ffe832c50e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Remora <noreply@localhost>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 12:57:48 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] statusbar: give the tuner's icon list an entry point again

LineageParts' Settings > System > Status bar > "System icons" fires an
implicit com.android.settings.action.STATUS_BAR_TUNER. Nothing in AOSP
declares it -- the action is a LineageOS SystemUI addition that
lineage-24.0 has not forward-ported -- and androidx Preference.performClick
calls startActivity with no try/catch, so the row is a hard crash:

  android.content.ActivityNotFoundException: No Activity found to handle
  Intent { act=com.android.settings.action.STATUS_BAR_TUNER }

The screen it wants still exists: tuner_prefs.xml keeps the whole
status_bar PreferenceScreen, and StatusBarSwitch still writes the
icon_blacklist secure setting -- which the Compose status bar honors again
since "statusbar: honor icon_blacklist in the Compose icon pipeline". Only
the route between the two was missing.

Route it through an activity-alias instead of enabling TunerActivity, so
the activity stays disabled and its EXTRA_SETTINGS filter does not add a
"System UI Tuner" tile to Settings. An alias of a disabled target still
resolves, as the .DemoMode alias has always done.

SubSettingsFragment cannot host this route -- it lifts its preferences out
of a parent TunerFragment found through getTargetFragment(), and an intent
entry has no parent -- so inflate the sub-screen by key instead.

Change-Id: I534ccf4aa1c2bb5172fbca946d2ae3ed79fc5389
---
 packages/SystemUI/AndroidManifest.xml         | 19 +++++++
 .../tuner/StatusBarTunerFragment.java         | 52 +++++++++++++++++++
 .../android/systemui/tuner/TunerActivity.java | 10 +++-
 3 files changed, 80 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/tuner/StatusBarTunerFragment.java

diff --git a/packages/SystemUI/AndroidManifest.xml b/packages/SystemUI/AndroidManifest.xml
index 1a5392dad2ac..313187a33b07 100644
--- a/packages/SystemUI/AndroidManifest.xml
+++ b/packages/SystemUI/AndroidManifest.xml
@@ -646,6 +646,25 @@
             </intent-filter>
         </activity-alias>
 
+        <!-- The tuner's status bar icon list, reachable on its own so that LineageParts'
+             Settings > System > Status bar > "System icons" resolves. Nothing in AOSP handles
+             STATUS_BAR_TUNER, so that preference is otherwise a fatal ActivityNotFoundException.
+             An alias rather than enabling TunerActivity: the activity stays disabled, so its
+             EXTRA_SETTINGS filter keeps its "System UI Tuner" tile out of Settings. An alias of a
+             disabled target still resolves, exactly as .DemoMode above already does. -->
+        <activity-alias android:name=".tuner.StatusBarTuner"
+                  android:targetActivity=".tuner.TunerActivity"
+                  android:icon="@drawable/tuner"
+                  android:theme="@style/TunerSettings"
+                  android:label="@string/status_bar"
+                  android:process=":tuner"
+                  android:exported="true">
+            <intent-filter>
+                <action android:name="com.android.settings.action.STATUS_BAR_TUNER" />
+                <category android:name="android.intent.category.DEFAULT" />
+            </intent-filter>
+        </activity-alias>
+
         <!-- Callback for invoking a smart action from the screenshot notification. -->
         <receiver android:name=".screenshot.SmartActionsReceiver"
                   android:exported="false"/>
diff --git a/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/tuner/StatusBarTunerFragment.java b/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/tuner/StatusBarTunerFragment.java
new file mode 100644
index 000000000000..a262143cfd64
--- /dev/null
+++ b/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/tuner/StatusBarTunerFragment.java
@@ -0,0 +1,52 @@
